.Dd November 10, 2026
.Dt UNAME 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm uname
.Nd print system identification
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl amnoprsv
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility writes selected fields of the system identification to standard output.
The fields are separated by a single space and the output ends with a newline.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl a
Print all of
.Fl s ,
.Fl n ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl v
and
.Fl m ,
in that order.
.It Fl m
Print the machine hardware name.
.It Fl n
Print the nodename.
.It Fl o
Print the operating system name
.Pq Dq RavenBSD .
.It Fl p
Print the processor type.
On RavenBSD this is the same value as
.Fl m .
.It Fl r
Print the operating system release.
.It Fl s
Print the operating system name.
.It Fl v
Print the operating system version.
.El
.Pp
With no options,
.Fl s
is assumed.
The fields are always written in the order
.Fl s ,
.Fl n ,
.Fl r ,
.Fl v ,
.Fl m ,
.Fl p ,
.Fl o ,
regardless of the order in which the options were given.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2.
A failure to read the system identification exits with status 1.
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fl amnrsv
options conform to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
The
.Fl o
and
.Fl p
options are NetBSD-compatible extensions.
